# K0 / B007 — Run 2 replica annotation (blind).

C R174 OL SEC-016,GOV-013 | MUST | Choose the authentication scheme by the actual application (Bearer/OIDC for an SPA calling an API; cookies for server-rendered apps; Identity when the app owns local users and needs account management; external OIDC/OAuth when identity is delegated); a User entity or profile management alone does not call for Identity, and an API needing authentication does not call for custom JWT issuance when an existing identity provider issues tokens. | Backend authentication | none stated
C R175 OL WF-015,GOV-014 | MUST | Build-fix restores the affected scope to green without hiding failures, weakening behavior or introducing unrelated changes. | Build/test repair | none stated
C R176 OL WF-013 | MUST | Reproduce and diagnose the actual failure (narrowest reproducing command with the repository's actual .slnx/projects; complete output read and grouped by root cause) before editing; no guessing; fix root causes and the highest-leverage cause first. | Build/test repair | none stated
C R177 OL WF-014 | MUST | Small bounded iterations: rerun the narrowest failing verification after each meaningful fix, expand only after the focused failure is resolved; stop and reassess when progress stalls (same root failure after different fixes, growing unrelated failures, incompatible toolchain, missing infrastructure, unresolvable package compatibility, undeterminable behavior); never repeat variants of the same failed guess. | Build/test repair | none stated
C R178 OL WF-015 | MUST NOT | Never weaken, delete, skip or suppress relevant tests, compiler, TypeScript, lint or analyzer failures merely to pass; do not weaken a strong assertion or delete/skip a failing test because fixing it is inconvenient. | Build/test repair | none stated
C R179 OL GOV-014,RUN-009,ARC-001 | MUST | Preserve architecture and project conventions while fixing; a green build obtained by violating architecture (e.g. Application -> Infrastructure references, DbContext in Application, business logic in a Controller, Angular-only authorization, scattered HTTP calls) is not a successful repair. | Build/test repair | none stated
C R180 OL WF-005,WF-007 | MUST | Determine the affected scope (backend, Angular, both, contract/client generation, dependencies, toolchain) and do not run unrelated build systems merely because they exist. | Build/test repair | none stated
C R181 OL WF-018 | MUST | For Angular inspect package.json first and use scripts that actually exist; do not invent script names or assume a test runner (an existing project may deliberately use another runner than the D-09 default). | Frontend build/test commands | Applies the CI-scoped WF-018 rule to local repair.
C R182 OL ARC-001 | MUST NOT | Never solve a dependency problem with an invalid project reference (e.g. Application -> Infrastructure). | Backend repair | none stated
C R183 OL WF-015,FE-001,DEP-014,DEP-015 | MUST NOT | Frontend repairs do not convert code to any to silence TypeScript, disable strict mode, suppress template diagnostics without understanding, add NgModules to work around standalone configuration problems, replace framework APIs speculatively, or add another state-management or HTTP library to bypass a local issue. | Frontend repair | none stated
C R184 OL WF-016,WF-013 | MUST | For full-stack/contract failures determine the authoritative contract; do not patch both sides into inconsistent shapes merely to compile; with OpenAPI generation verify the backend contract, regenerate the client normally, review the generated changes, then fix handwritten frontend code. | Contract failures | none stated
C R185 OL GOV-014 | MUST | If expected behavior intentionally changed, update the test to express the new contract and confirm the change was actually requested. | Test failures | none stated
C R186 OL DEP-006,DEP-007 | MUST | During package-related repair respect Central Package Management and do not delete package-lock.json reflexively. | Dependency failures | none stated
C R187 OL GOV-014,WF-013 | MUST | For upgrade fallout distinguish compile errors from runtime behavior changes, check official migration documentation, update obsolete APIs deliberately (no fabricated replacement APIs when they can be verified), preserve architecture/behavior and perform no additional unrelated upgrade. | Framework/API upgrades | none stated
C R188 OL GOV-014,DEP-008,WF-009 | MUST NOT | Do not change the repository's declared SDK, Node, framework or language version merely because the local machine differs; report an unavailable toolchain instead of editing source to compensate. | Toolchain problems | none stated
C R189 OL WF-016 | DEFAULT | When generated output is wrong or its source changed, fix the authoritative source (OpenAPI document, generator input, EF Core model, build configuration) and regenerate; do not manually patch disposable generated output unless intentionally maintained as source. | Generated code | Output intentionally maintained as source.
C R190 OL GOV-014,WF-008 | MUST | If a fix introduces new failures decide whether they reveal a legitimate dependency or revert/correct the fix; never leave the repository knowingly worse; do not clean up unrelated pre-existing failures unless they block verification or the user asks. | Build/test repair | Blocking or requested cleanup.
C R191 OL WF-005,WF-003,TST-010 | MUST | A repair is complete when the affected scope is green (builds, affected tests, consistent contracts, no known new regression, no accidental workaround); diagnosis probes follow verify § 4; then run verify for the final pass when appropriate. | Build/test repair completion | none stated
C R192 OL WF-009 | MUST | Report repairs with backend build, frontend build and tests as PASS / NOT RUN / NOT APPLICABLE plus failure, root cause, changes and remaining issues; do not claim the problem is fixed while a known relevant failure remains. | Build/test repair report | none stated
C X26 EX RUN-021,ARC-017 | AVOID (listed common mistake) | Caching EF tracked entities across Unit of Work boundaries is listed as a mistake to avoid. | Caching persistence data | none stated | No oracle policy and no K0 standard forbids caching tracked entities across Unit of Work scopes; the knowledge skill adds this restriction as a named mistake. | A cache that holds EF-tracked entity instances across requests is treated as a defect.
C R193 OL WF-007 | MUST NOT | An optional local formatter does not become a mandatory CI gate without the project adopting that policy. | CI pipelines | none stated
C R194 OL WF-018 | MUST | Frontend CI runs the unit-test and lint scripts the workspace actually defines, adding them only when the project defines them. | Frontend CI | none stated
C R195 OL TST-004,GOV-013 | MUST | Provide CI test services (SQL Server, PostgreSQL, Redis, brokers) only when tests require them; the generic template hardcodes no database provider and the test environment stays isolated from Development and Production data. | CI test infrastructure | none stated
C R196 OL DEP-003,DEP-004 | MUST NOT | Automatic dependency updates in CI need explicit adoption; dependency-audit findings are treated per the project's security policy. | CI pipelines | Explicitly adopted automation.
C R197 OL DEP-018 | MUST NOT | Store or publish only artifacts later stages need; build and publish container images from CI only when container deployment is part of the project. | CI artifacts | none stated
C R198 OL WF-019 | MUST | Migration scripts or bundles may be generated in CI and are executed by an explicit deployment step. | Deployment | none stated

